    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#951;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> is the efficiency of an engine at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>447</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>147</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi>C</mi></math> while <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#951;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> is the efficiency at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>947</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>47</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>. The ratio <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>&#951;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>&#951;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></math> will be",
